                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d44b89e-cb94-3fb1-87df-8b3e805ada23",
                        "entry_id": "65bae6d5-4316-3e8d-93ea-9788a0a640b9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "eine in Kenia und Tansania gesprochene Bantusprache"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a0ea4c3-6ab0-468b-9cff-54f4a7ea8654",
                                "sense_id": "7d44b89e-cb94-3fb1-87df-8b3e805ada23",
                                "text": "Hast Du in Afrika auch Kisuaheli gelernt?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5e2adb1-2f0c-4e24-b5d3-51146a3fd979",
                                "sense_id": "7d44b89e-cb94-3fb1-87df-8b3e805ada23",
                                "text": "„Alle Vorhaltungen, Überzeugungsversuche und Bitten halfen nichts, der Doktor blieb unbeirrbar und lernte in seiner Freizeit seelenruhig Arabisch, Kisuaheli und Mandingo-Dialekte.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bb16b68-0cd5-4bae-9864-1a52f805cfc8",
                                "sense_id": "7d44b89e-cb94-3fb1-87df-8b3e805ada23",
                                "text": "„Johanna Sarre, die fließend Kisuaheli spricht, hat zwei Monate im Slum gewohnt und Feldforschung direkt vor Ort betrieben.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0d058333-8fa4-4d8a-8f32-d173c82204db",
                        "source_entry_id": "65bae6d5-4316-3e8d-93ea-9788a0a640b9",
                        "source_sense_id": "7d44b89e-cb94-3fb1-87df-8b3e805ada23",
                        "source_sense_description": "eine in Kenia und Tansania gesprochene Bantusprache",
                        "target_lang_word": "Swahili",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Swahili",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1cae3d26-676e-3b80-932b-f463c3abe265",
                                        "entry_id": "913ee5df-6f4a-3c72-bb88-558fc9948c04",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An agglutinative language of the Bantu branch widely spoken in East Africa. Born in its modern form from the hybridization of the Arabic and Bantu cultures, it was the language of the traders in East Africa, and spread along the routes of trade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6867caf-aef1-4039-9477-8feb64aa2960",
                                                "sense_id": "1cae3d26-676e-3b80-932b-f463c3abe265",
                                                "text": "On Tuesday night at the Club Serene in Brooklyn, Mayor Koch proclaimed Kwanzaa Week in New York. Then he told the crowd of about 400 that he had practiced his Swahili in order to pronounce correctly such exotic-sounding words as kujichagulia (self-determination), ujamaa (cooperative economics) and imani (faith), the theme of Kwanzaa '83."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11fd2053-2f7e-4abe-8396-a60e230743de",
                                                "sense_id": "1cae3d26-676e-3b80-932b-f463c3abe265",
                                                "text": "Similarly, Swahili evolved as the trading language in East Africa and is described as having an Arab vocabulary upon an African grammar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Swahili",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f9f556f-4589-3475-9a7d-4bf42159ac87",
                                        "entry_id": "0c94a234-e385-3da6-b9bc-51842b5c05ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of various ethnic groups — mainly Bantu, Afro-Arab and Comorian — inhabiting the Swahili coast."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d19bdd4-b66c-4fce-88c9-7eb1035ce33d",
                                                "sense_id": "9f9f556f-4589-3475-9a7d-4bf42159ac87",
                                                "text": "The Swahilis are a unique and important community that began to form before the arrival of Islam, as a result of intermarriage between Arab traders who came to the coast and women from local ethnic groups."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96ed8aa2-9868-4e69-9302-98e3ca0741f2",
                                                "sense_id": "9f9f556f-4589-3475-9a7d-4bf42159ac87",
                                                "text": "The final sources for the early history of the Swahili are the oral traditions related by them about their own past."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d25dcbeb-01b3-4bd3-b8b9-1f962f95dfba",
                        "source_entry_id": "65bae6d5-4316-3e8d-93ea-9788a0a640b9",
                        "source_sense_id": "7d44b89e-cb94-3fb1-87df-8b3e805ada23",
                        "source_sense_description": "eine in Kenia und Tansania gesprochene Bantusprache",
                        "target_lang_word": "kiswahili",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "kiswahili",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ed2c83d-138a-3807-96de-a6ec7ff5e3f3",
                                        "entry_id": "b46eee23-860c-3ac6-9c68-d890bd620991",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Langue vernaculaire bantoue parlée en Afrique orientale, et influencée par l’arabe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6aa0cc79-d77b-4ce5-8b5a-ec05b2797805",
                                                "sense_id": "3ed2c83d-138a-3807-96de-a6ec7ff5e3f3",
                                                "text": "Après quelques heures passées sur le sol dans un état semi-conscient, Fred Bosire entend parler kiswahili et repère des bottes de l’armée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "123f47a4-3ff2-4a82-8396-260e90f93b32",
                                                "sense_id": "3ed2c83d-138a-3807-96de-a6ec7ff5e3f3",
                                                "text": "Perchée à l’extrême nord-est du pays, aux frontières de l’Ouganda, du Soudan et de l’Éthiopie, Kakuma se traduit par «nulle part» en kiswahili."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3105ba18-adda-4118-94ee-cb8471e2c358",
                                                "sense_id": "3ed2c83d-138a-3807-96de-a6ec7ff5e3f3",
                                                "text": "Si, pour la première fois, la finale n’opposera pas l’Europe à l’Amérique du Sud, c’est avant tout l’œuvre de Moïse Katumbi Chapwe, président inspiré du TP Mazembe (« les corbeaux », en kiswahili)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b78f4e6b-310f-4910-bdcb-09f01f180f94",
                                                "sense_id": "3ed2c83d-138a-3807-96de-a6ec7ff5e3f3",
                                                "text": "Le jour du jugement, ignorant les menaces physiques et malgré l’inaction des forces de police, elles ont défilé de leur foyer au tribunal en criant « haki yangu », « j’exige que l’on respecte mes droits » en kiswahili. Et le juge a rendu sa décision: les filles ont gagné ! https://secure.avaaz.org/fr/tak_kaias_win_global_loc_fr/?bNZYtab&v=31194"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
